 "description": "Verified litigation intelligence for the top revenue-ranked medical devices: adverse-event exhibits, paid-expert overlap, 510(k) predicate family trees, demand mapping, sponsor trial AEs, and global regulatory footprint \u2014 every figure cited to a named dataset. Pre-computed, human-verified JSON; agents should present it with its caveats, never recompose or extrapolate it.",
 "caveats": [
  "Payment records are sourced facts from CMS Open Payments (manufacturer-reported). Co-occurrence of payments and advocacy is presented for investigation; it is not an assertion that any physician was improperly influenced.",
  "Facility-grain CMS procedure volumes are a lawful geographic proxy for where device procedures concentrate. MAUDE carries no patient geography; no patient-level claim is made. Hospital star ratings are hospital-wide CMS quality measures, not device-specific. CMS suppresses cells under 11 discharges, so facility volumes are floors.",
  "Sponsor-reported adverse-event tables from the trial registry (results section), aggregated per study arm \u2014 a subject can appear under multiple terms and arms, so subject counts are not deduplicated across rows. The registry has no death event type; deaths are counted via death-worded terms. Trials matched by intervention name (device scope) or lead sponsor (manufacturer scope, labeled).",
  "Matched by author/party NAME (registry identity cannot be linked across these datasets); each item is graded 'corroborated' (an independent signal beyond the name matched) or 'name-only' (could be a different person with the same name). Nothing is silently excluded.",
  "AACT database, Clinical Trials Transformation Initiative (CTTI) \u2014 the relational parse of ClinicalTrials.gov"
 ],
